 "expected": "not_yet",
 "why": "Near miss: Blender materials lesson 3 (\"A Noise Texture feeds a Color Ramp that feeds the material's Base Color\"). The learner first dragged Noise Color straight into Base Color, then added the Color Ramp after it and wired Noise Fac -> Color Ramp Fac, but dropped the Color Ramp's Color on Roughness instead of Base Color. Both nodes exist and something feeds Base Color (the raw noise), but the ramp only drives roughness, so the marble colours the ramp sets never show.",
 "step": {
  "id": "s3",
  "index": 3,
  "title": "Build a material from nodes",
  "file": "marble.blend",
  "instructions": "Select the sphere and open the Shading workspace. Add a Noise Texture (Shift+A > Texture > Noise Texture) and a Color Ramp (Shift+A > Converter > Color Ramp). Connect the Noise's Fac to the Color Ramp's Fac and the Color Ramp's Color to the Principled BSDF's Base Color. Save (Cmd+S).",
